    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5ae3ab72_231ac1c4",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/config_chip-npcx9.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 110,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132339
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-02T04:57:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This could be `#define NPCX_PROGRAM_MEMORY_SIZE (416 * 1024)`\nThe npcx firmware binary image in the flash should be composed of `firmware image header + firmware image`.\nIn npcx9m3f, the RO/RW flash size is 256KB (i.e. 512/2). The first 4KB is reserved for the `firmware image header`. This means the program memory size need to be (256KB - 4KB)\nIn npcx9m8s, the flash size is 1MB (512KB for RO and 512KB for RW).\nAs 416 KB is far from 512 KB, we don\u0027t have to reduce 4KB for the NPCX_PROGRAM_MEMORY_SIZE in npcx9m8s.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 110,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 110,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "36547c262227ffd1358a4a4e02c500538a495f9e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fa4eed55_b073fcab",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/config_chip-npcx9.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 110,
      "author": {
        "id": 1529242
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-17T20:28:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e As 416 KB is far from 512 KB, we don\u0027t have to reduce 4KB for the NPCX_PROGRAM_MEMORY_SIZE in npcx9m8s\n\nThis might be a strange question but why are we reducing the program memory size from 512 KB to 416 KB?",
      "parentUuid": "5ae3ab72_231ac1c4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 110,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 110,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "36547c262227ffd1358a4a4e02c500538a495f9e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cf53419d_712c6e77",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/config_chip-npcx9.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 110,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132339
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-18T01:53:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi Bobby,\nLet me explain how the EC firmware is loaded and execute at initialization to answer your question:\nThe EC firmware is programed to the EC\u0027s internal SPI flash.\nAfter EC power-up, the boot loader (in ROM) copies the EC image from the internal SPI flash to the code RAM (416 KB in npcx998fs) and executes the code in the RAM.\nAs the EC code is executed in the CODE RAM (in order to get the better performance), the program memory size is limited to the CODE RAM size but the SPI flash size.",
      "parentUuid": "fa4eed55_b073fcab",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 110,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 110,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "36547c262227ffd1358a4a4e02c500538a495f9e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3c5eb4df_a46f210d",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/config_chip-npcx9.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 110,
      "author": {
        "id": 1529242
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-20T21:54:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, thanks for the response, that clarifies a lot of things! I didn\u0027t notice that the application was running out of RAM in this case. I\u0027m a little concerned about the impact on free RAM space. Based on present numbers it looks like we should be okay but we\u0027ll need to keep an eye on that. \n\nHow significant do you anticipate the impact of running from FLASH would be?",
      "parentUuid": "cf53419d_712c6e77",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 110,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 110,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "36547c262227ffd1358a4a4e02c500538a495f9e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
